{
  "id": "bigville_office",
  "version": "1.2.0",
  "depends_on": [],
  "self_load_only": true,
  "description": "bigville R48 (block 358000): JOBS/ROLES ARE AGENT-CREATED, ADVERTISED, APPLIED-FOR, APPOINTED, DELEGATED -- never hardcoded, never magically filled. CREATE: of_council_create (only via a DECREE -- the council's bureaucracy: 'more police', 'a tax collector') / of_owner_create (an OWNER directly, when an establishment's workload exceeds capacity -- the overloaded innkeeper conceives a cook). MAKE IT KNOWN: an opening is not magically known -- it is ADVERTISED (a posted Notice heard by residents, of_hear_notice), spread by WORD OF MOUTH through `knows` ties (of_word_of_mouth), or the creator directly ASKS a person (adapter makes them aware). APPLY: an aware agent DECIDES whether to apply -- a collapse {apply,pass} valued by want_work - reservation (a job-seeker applies, a content person passes; you cannot be appointed to a job you did not apply for). SELECT: the delegator chooses among the APPLICANTS (Argmax by w_competence*competence + w_loyalty*loyalty -- bodies diverge), of_install appoints the choice (one office per person). DELEGATE: the holder's authority IS the delegator's (constable wields the council's; lose recognition, lose it). VACATE/SUCCEED: a holder who dies/leaves vacates; the office outlives him and the opening is re-advertised for a successor (falls-down-a-well safe). of_revoke removes a holder. Composes with bigville_recognition (council authority) and the council decree machinery. v1.2.0: office advertising is WIRED TO THE NOTICEBOARD -- of_hear_posted: a resident who READ a posted job-note advertising an office (bigville_noticeboard) becomes aware of the opening. Advertising a role posts a physical Note on the square's board; visitors read it and learn of the job (the abstract of_hear_notice remains for the note-less demonstrator).",
  "nodes": [],
  "edges": [],
  "productions": [],
  "concepts": [],
  "rules": [
    {
